Relevant columns & their potential usage
• YEAR._2017  
  – "type": filter to only `"WatchEvent"` records.  
  – "repo":"name": repository’s full name, to group the events.  
  – "actor":"id" (or "actor":"login"): unique watcher identifier, to count distinct watchers.  

• GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_FILES  
  – "repo_name": repository name; use it to INNER‑JOIN so that only repos also present in the code snapshot are returned.

Typical conditions we will need  
• WHERE t."type" = 'WatchEvent'  
• GROUP BY repo_name HAVING COUNT(DISTINCT watcher_id) > 300  
• ORDER BY watcher_cnt DESC LIMIT 2  

